WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.050 --> 00:00:03.325
Migration ends on a
date; certificates don't.

2
00:00:03.325 --> 00:00:08.506
Public TLS validity falls to forty-seven
days from March 15, 2029, and the

3
00:00:08.506 --> 00:00:14.038
design rule is that no certificate may
depend on a person remembering a date.

4
00:00:14.038 --> 00:00:19.005
So the target has three renewal engines:
Intune profiles for managed devices,

5
00:00:19.005 --> 00:00:21.955
AD CS autoenrollment
for domain controllers,

6
00:00:21.955 --> 00:00:27.312
and CyberArk Certificate Manager for server
certificates, each with a named owner.

7
00:00:27.312 --> 00:00:30.074
Neither Microsoft issuer offers ACME,

8
00:00:30.074 --> 00:00:35.425
so the lifecycle platform provides it,
on its own servers outside FIPS mode.

9
00:00:35.425 --> 00:00:38.767
Drift checks run at least weekly
and are kept as evidence,

10
00:00:38.767 --> 00:00:42.037
because an assessor asks how
long a finding stayed open.

11
00:00:42.037 --> 00:00:46.105
And treat a mismatched identifier in
a certificate as a security event,

12
00:00:46.105 --> 00:00:49.610
because it can mean the certificate
went to a different user.
